Comment		=> 'Percolation rates are determined by the soil drainage category in the FAO/UNESCO (2003) soil map of the world: http://www.fao.org/soils-portal/soil-survey/soil-maps-and-databases/faounesco-soil-map-of-the-world/en/.  Conversion of soil drainage category to rice paddy percolation rates is described in: Wisser D, S Frolking, EM Douglas, BM Fekete, CJ Vörösmarty, AH Schumann (2008) Global irrigation water demand: Variability and uncertainties arising from agricultural and climate data sets, Geophysical Research Letters, 35, L24408, doi:10.1029/2008GL035296.' 
